Titre$ Lepista Danemark
com$cf http://www.mycokey.com/AU / adapt GF aout 2013


1,0 $ All parts whitish to bluish-grey $ L. glaucocana (not known from Denmark)
1,2 $ Fruitbody darker with brown or violet colours
2,3 $ With violet, bluish or lilac colours on cap, stem or gills
2,5 $ Without violet, bluish or lilac colours
3,0 $ With lilac colours on stem, cap and gills pale brownish. $ L. saeva
3,4 $ Stem and gills with violet, bluish or lilac colours, cap brown to violet
4,0 $ Stem 0.5-1 cm thick, cap hygrophanous, smell weak, sp. 5.5-7 x 3.5-4 µm $ L. sordida
4,0 $ Stem 1-2.5 cm thick, cap normally not hygrophanous, smell aromatic or gass-like, sp. 6-8.5 x 4-5 µm. $ L. nuda
5,6 $ Gills adnate to emarginate
5,7 $ Gills decurrent
6,0 $ Cap greyish brown, often with darker spots near the margin, smell weak, in dry grassland, sp. 5-6.5 x 3.5-5 µm. $ L. luscina
6,0 $ Cap yellowish brown to cinnamon-buff, without dark spots, smell aromatic, ecology different, sp. 6.5-9 x 4-5 µm. $ L. irina
7,8 $ Cap yellowish brown, not hygrophanous but possibly with darker spots, sp. almost globose, 3.5-4 µm
7,9 $ Cap liver brown to greyish brown, hygrophanous, sp. ellipsoid, 5.5-9 x 3.5-5 µm
8,0 $ Cap without darker spots, yellowish brown to reddish brown. $ L. flaccida
8,0 $ Cap with darker spots, cream to pale yellowish brown. $ L. gilva
9,0 $ Stem pale, whitish, cap smooth, not fibrillose, without darker spots. $ L. ovispora
9,0 $ Stem greyish to brownish like the cap, cap fibrillose, at least near the margin, often with darker spots. $ L. multiformis (not known from Denmark)
